# Add this line to the droplet's existing crontab (crontab -e) alongside
# everything else already there. No API key needed -- GOES-18 GLM data on
# AWS Open Data is unauthenticated.
#
# Hourly, not "once right after midnight Pacific" -- publish_daily.py is
# idempotent per Pacific calendar date (tracks the last date it rotated
# for in state/last_rotation_date.txt), so running it hourly means
# whichever tick is first to land after midnight PT does that day's
# rotation+fetch+render, and every other tick that day is a fast no-op.
# This sidesteps needing a DST-aware UTC cron time to stay "shortly after
# midnight PT" year-round.

15 * * * * /opt/ingalls-weather-scripts/columbia-basin-lightning-daily-map/venv/bin/python3 /opt/ingalls-weather-scripts/columbia-basin-lightning-daily-map/deploy/publish_daily.py >> /opt/ingalls-weather-scripts/columbia-basin-lightning-daily-map/state/cron.log 2>&1
